<title>USA: Sallie Mae prices floating-rate note issue.</title>
<headline>Sallie Mae prices floating-rate note issue.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Student Loan Marketing Association said Monday it had priced a $500 million issue of short-term floating-rate notes at 21 basis points above the 91-day U.S. Treasury bill.</p>
<p>When-issued trading is expected to begin at 0820 EDT/1220 GMT Tuesday, it said.</p>
<p>The notes are for settlement August 21. Maturity date is February 19, 1998. Cusip number is 86387TFE3.</p>
<p>The interest rate on the notes will be reset the day after each weekly bill auction.</p>
</text>
